# Everything here is DELETED from $HOME on every host that applies, and
# bin/chezmoi-update fans out to five accounts across three machines. Keep
# entries explicit and narrow.
#
# NOTE: do not add `*~` back here. .chezmoiignore matches editor backups, and an
# ignored path is skipped by every target-state operation including removal, so
# a `*~` rule here is silently dead. It was in this file for a long time and
# never once deleted anything -- ~/.bashrc~ was matched by both files and
# survived. .chezmoiignore already stops backups from ever deploying; clearing
# out ones that predate that fix is a one-time `rm`, not chezmoi's job.
DEADJOE
.config/fish/themes/Catppuccin Mocha.theme
.config/fish/themes/Catppuccin Macchiato.theme
.config/ghostty/config.ghostty
.bashrc.d/chezmoi-completion.sh
.config/neofetch
.config/hyfetch.json
